<title>USA: Full service is restored to SEC EDGAR computer.</title>
<headline>Full service is restored to SEC EDGAR computer.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Securities and Exchange Commission said Monday as of 0800 EST/1300 GMT its main electronic filing computer system was fully operational.</p>
<p>All filings are to be submitted to SEC's primary Electronic Data Gathering Analysis and Retrival (EDGAR) system located in Alexandria, Va., the commission said in a statement.</p>
<p>A power failure to the main computer resulted in a major system failure which precluded it from being able to receive, process or disseminate electronic filings on March 21.</p>
</text>
